        :rulingText """To resolve Nezumi Informant’s ability in a multiplayer game, the next opponent in turn order (or, if it’s an opponent’s turn, the opponent whose turn it is) chooses a card in hand and sets it aside without revealing it. Then each other opponent in turn order does the same. Finally, all chosen cards are revealed and discarded at the same time."""@en ] .

:PileOn rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Pile On" ;
    :manaCost "{3}{B}" ;
    :manaValue "4"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Instant ;
    :hasRarity :Rare ;
    :hasColor :Black ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Black ;
    :isInSet :MarchOfTheMachine ;
    :cardNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Javier Charro" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :hasKeywordAction :Surveil ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Convoke ;
    :printedText """Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)
Destroy target creature or planeswalker. Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)"""@en ;
    :oracleText """Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)
Destroy target creature or planeswalker. Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)"""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=607159"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/mom/122/pile-on"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :isAvailableOn :PaperMagic ,
                   :MTGArena ,
                   :MagicOnline ;
    :arenaId "84395"^^xsd:positiveInteger ;
    :arenaName "Pile On" ;
    :arenaSetCode "MOM" ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Historic ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Timeless ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Alchemy ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Brawl ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :StandardBrawl ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a creature you control has a mana ability with {T} in the cost, activating that ability while casting a spell with convoke will result in the creature being tapped before you pay the spell's costs. You won't be able to tap it again for convoke. Similarly, if you sacrifice a creature to activate a mana ability while casting a spell with convoke, that creature won't be on the battlefield when you pay the spell's costs, so you won't be able to tap it for convoke."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You perform the actions stated on a card in sequence. For some spells and abilities, you'll surveil last. For others, you'll surveil and then perform other actions."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Tapping a multicolored creature using convoke will pay for {1} or one mana of your choice of any of that creature's colors."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Tapping an untapped creature that's attacking or blocking to convoke a spell won't cause that creature to stop attacking or blocking."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """When calculating a spell's total cost, include any alternative costs, additional costs, or anything else that increases or reduces the cost to cast the spell. Convoke applies after the total cost is calculated. Convoke doesn't change a spell's mana cost or mana value."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You can tap any untapped creature you control to convoke a spell, even one you haven't controlled continuously since the beginning of your most recent turn."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """When you surveil, you may put all the cards you look at back on top of your library, you may put all of those cards into your graveyard, or you may put some of those cards on top and the rest of them into your graveyard."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-01-12"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Because convoke isn't an alternative cost, it can be used in conjunction with alternative costs."""@en ] .

